ss="sc-9ed2d16a-0 sc-b1a93422-0 EBMGw bxETTS"><div class="sc-d3b1f0c-0 sc-d3b1f0c-1 fqoDra ferUGe"><div class="sc-d3b1f0c-0 sc-d3b1f0c-1 sc-b1a93422-2 htvGag faHCM gRGlIF"><img src="/static/images/collective-navigation/CollectiveNavbarIconAbout.png" alt="" class="sc-b1a93422-1 dWuXCV"/></div><div class="sc-d3b1f0c-0 sc-d3b1f0c-1 kelEPL fHSAwH"><h2 data-cy="category-ABOUT-title" font-size="32px" font-weight="normal" color="black.900" class="sc-1709896-0 bWUsCp">About</h2></div><hr class="sc-d0d050d8-0 hGzNES"/></div></div><section id="section-about" data-cy="section-about" class="sc-3340244f-0 iTPjmR"><div class="sc-9ed2d16a-0 sc-7355880b-0 cIqaQH"><div class="sc-9ed2d16a-0 eRmECd"><div class="sc-9ed2d16a-0 jRaTqn"><div><div data-cy="longDescription" font-size="14px" class="sc-63bf996f-0 bKpumw sc-63bf996f-2 joDdkz"><div><a href="https://opencollective.com/redirect?url=https%3A%2F%2Fbrew.sh%2F">Homebrew</a> is an open-source, free package manager for macOS, Linux and Windows (with the Windows Subsystem for Linux).<br/><br/></div><div>Homebrew is a non-profit project run entirely by volunteers. We need your funds to pay for software, hardware, hosting around continuous integration, maintainer contributions, travel to conferences and future improvements to the project. Every donation will be spent on making Homebrew better for our users.</div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section id="section-our-team" data-cy="section-our-team" class="sc-3340244f-0 eGKBUl"><div class="sc-9ed2d16a-0 sc-7355880b-0 jyulmr"><div class="sc-9ed2d16a-0 uzGKt"><h2 font-weight="500" color="black.700" class="sc-dcb94ee2-0 sc-dcb94ee2-5 kmgLsS">Our team</h2><div class="sc-9ed2d16a-0 bGxwtX"><div width="144" height="auto" class="sc-2c35d607-0 sc-d82cae7-0 bfQJEs gMcYKv"><div class="sc-d82cae7-1 jfGyLV"><div class="sc-d3b1f0c-0 inLDtj"><a href="/mikemcquaid"><div style="background-image:url(https://images.opencollective.com/mikemcquaid/18b9eb8/avatar.png);background-size:cover" size="64"